% Test cases for the patient lifts policy (patient_lifts.le): synthetic
% claims, one per criterion of LCD L33799 and per benefit point of Policy
% Article A52516. Findings are recorded as the treating practitioner's, a
% medical reviewer's or the Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the
% answer conditional. A patient lift is rented: the first month's claim is
% shown, with no continued need to document.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base patient_lifts cases includes these resources:
    patient_lifts.

the knowledge base patient_lifts cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete first-month claim for a hydraulic lift (E0630): the two
% findings, the standard written order communicated before the date of
% service, the delivery and its proof.
scenario hydraulic_lift_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the lift.
    the HCPCS code of the lift is "E0630".
    the lift is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding bed to chair transfer required about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "transfers to a wheelchair for meals and toileting".
    the finding bed confined without lift about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "paraplegia; the caregiver cannot lift the beneficiary".
    the order for the lift is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the lift is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the lift includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the lift includes order date.
    the order for the lift includes description of the item.
    the order for the lift includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the lift includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the lift was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the lift was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the lift.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% An electric lift (E0635): the same basic criteria (the LCD text cited
% covers it as it covers the hydraulic lift).
scenario electric_lift is:
    claim 1 is for the electric lift.
    the HCPCS code of the electric lift is "E0635".
    the electric lift is furnished to Ben.
    the finding bed to chair transfer required about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding bed confined without lift about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The first basic criterion fails: the medical reviewer finds no transfer
% between bed and chair is required.
scenario no_transfer_required is:
    claim 1 is for the lift.
    the HCPCS code of the lift is "E0630".
    the lift is furnished to Cy.
    the residence of Cy is private residence.
    the finding bed to chair transfer required about Cy is unsupported, according to the medical reviewer, because "the record documents the beneficiary walking to the bathroom with a walker".
    the finding bed confined without lift about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% The second basic criterion: the Council finds the record does not show
% the beneficiary would be bed confined without a lift.
scenario not_bed_confined_council is:
    claim 1 is for the lift.
    the HCPCS code of the lift is "E0630".
    the lift is furnished to Dee.
    the finding bed to chair transfer required about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding bed confined without lift about Dee is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the home health notes show the beneficiary transferred to a chair daily by one aide with a gait belt before the lift was delivered".
    rn expects answers [].

% A multi-positional transfer system (E0636): with supine positioning
% required, covered; for a beneficiary who transfers seated, not decided —
% conditional on that finding.
scenario multi_positional is:
    claim 1 is for the transfer system.
    the HCPCS code of the transfer system is "E0636".
    the transfer system is furnished to Eve.
    the finding bed to chair transfer required about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding bed confined without lift about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding supine positioning required for transfers about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "unstable spine after a fracture; no sitting transfers".
    claim 2 is for the second transfer system.
    the HCPCS code of the second transfer system is "E1035".
    the second transfer system is furnished to Fay.
    the finding bed to chair transfer required about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding bed confined without lift about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding supine positioning required for transfers about Fay is established"].

% A replacement sling (E0621) for a covered lift, and one that is not a
% replacement for any lift.
scenario replacement_sling is:
    claim 1 is for the sling.
    the HCPCS code of the sling is "E0621".
    the sling is a replacement for a component of the lift.
    the sling is furnished to Ann.
    the HCPCS code of the lift is "E0630".
    the lift is furnished to Ann.
    the finding bed to chair transfer required about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding bed confined without lift about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    claim 2 is for the second sling.
    the HCPCS code of the second sling is "E0621".
    the second sling is furnished to Ann.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A toilet or tub lift (E0625): in scope, outside the benefit — the claim
% fails at applicability.
scenario toilet_tub_lift is:
    claim 1 is for the tub lift.
    the HCPCS code of the tub lift is "E0625".
    the tub lift is furnished to Gus.
    the residence of Gus is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].

% Reasonable and necessary, but no proof of delivery: payable fails at the
% remedy.
scenario no_proof_of_delivery is:
    claim 1 is for the lift.
    the HCPCS code of the lift is "E0630".
    the lift is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding bed to chair transfer required about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding bed confined without lift about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the lift is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the lift is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the lift includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the lift includes order date.
    the order for the lift includes description of the item.
    the order for the lift includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the lift includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the lift was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the lift was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the supplier holds proof of delivery for the lift"]].
